"Written by Claude from the measurements above. An interpretation, not a measurement.": "由 Claude 根據上面的測量結果撰寫。這是解讀，不是測量。",
"Barnard's Star is a small, cool red dwarf about 6 light-years away, and it moves across our sky faster than any other star. WANDERERS measured it shifting 170 arcseconds between 2010 and 2026, a speed of 10.55 arcseconds per year, within 1.5% of Gaia's 10.39. Confidence is high: all three key checks passed. The star is too bright for SPHEREx. All 242 measurements are flagged, so there is no reliable spectrum. Its brightness looked steady (−0.00 ± 0.04 mag), but that came only from the star's outer glow, so it's uncertain.": "巴納德星是一顆小而冷的紅矮星，距離我們約 6 光年，它在天空中移動得比其他任何恆星都快。WANDERERS 測得它在 2010 年到 2026 年間移動了 170 角秒，速度為每年 10.55 角秒，與 Gaia 的 10.39 相差不到 1.5%。可信度很高：三項關鍵檢查全部通過。這顆星對 SPHEREx 來説太亮了。全部 242 次測量都被標記，所以沒有可靠的光譜。它的亮度看起來很穩定（−0.00 ± 0.04 mag），但這隻來自恆星的外圍光暈，所以並不確定。",
