"16 billion": "160 億",
"infrared detections, searched for anything that moves.": "次紅外探測，在其中搜尋任何會移動的東西。",
"NASA's NEOWISE telescope photographed every part of the sky about every six months for ten years. We cut the sky into 12,288 equal tiles and, tile by tile, a program links each source's detections across the years, measures how far and how steadily it moves, throws out artefacts, and checks ESA's Gaia catalogue: a mover that Gaia already knows is explained. Then SPHEREx, which mapped the whole sky again in 2025–26, gets a say: the program reads SPHEREx's all-sky spectral cube at the spot where each unexplained mover should be by then, checks that it is there (and gone from where it was in 2014), and takes its 0.75–5 µm spectrum, looking for the methane dip and red colour of a cold brown dwarf. Whatever is left is ranked, so people can look at the most promising candidates first. A candidate is a lead, never a discovery.": "NASA 的 NEOWISE 望遠鏡用十年時間，大約每六個月拍一遍天空的每個部分。我們把天空切成 12,288 個相同大小的圖塊，再逐塊讓程式把每個源在多年間的探測連起來，測量它移動了多遠、移動得多穩，剔除偽影，並對照 ESA 的 Gaia 星表：Gaia 已經知道的移動天體就算是已解釋的。接着輪到 SPHEREx，它在 2025–26 年又給全天空測繪了一遍：程式在每個未解釋移動天體此時應該所在的位置讀取 SPHEREx 的全天光譜立方體，檢查它是否在那裏（並且已不在 2014 年的位置），再取出它 0.75–5 µm 的光譜，尋找冷褐矮星的甲烷吸收凹陷和紅色。剩下的會被排序，讓人們先看最有希望的候選體。候選體是線索，不是發現。",
"NEOWISE measures the motion (2014–2024). SPHEREx has no source catalogue yet, so the program measures its DR1 cube directly; its ~13″ pixels confirm only fast motions (about 1″ a year or more) and can blend close neighbours.": "NEOWISE 測量運動（2014–2024）。SPHEREx 還沒有源星表，所以程式直接測量它的 DR1 立方體；它約 13″ 的像素只能確認快速運動（每年約 1″ 或更多），也可能把靠近的鄰居混在一起。",
"Detections searched": "已搜尋的探測",
"7,593,273,577 passed the quality cuts": "7,593,273,577 個通過了質素篩選",
"Sources linked across years": "跨年份連接的源",
