"RW Aurigae is a young star about {0} light-years away that dims unpredictably behind clouds of dust. WANDERERS found no measurable motion between {1} and {2}. Gaia lists only {3} arcseconds per year, too small to see. From September {4} to September {5} its brightness changed by +{6} ± {7} magnitudes, which is within the uncertainty, so it looked steady. A few snapshots can still miss dimming that happens between them. Confidence is medium because the star is too bright for SPHEREx, and {8} of {9} measurements are flagged as saturated.": "RW Aurigae 是一顆年輕恆星，約 {0} 光年遠，會在塵埃雲後面不可預測地變暗。WANDERERS 發現它在 {1} 與 {2} 之間沒有可測運動。Gaia 只記錄了每年 {3} 角秒，小到看不出來。從 {4} 年9月到 {5} 年9月，它的亮度變化了 +{6} ± {7} 星等，在不確定度之內，所以看起來穩定。幾張快照仍可能漏掉它們之間發生的變暗。置信度為中等，因為這顆星對 SPHEREx 太亮，{9} 次測量中有 {8} 次因飽和被標記。",
